---
// The approved landing page. Styles: src/styles/landing.css. Behaviour: src/scripts/landing.js (bundled by Astro).
import '../styles/landing.css';
import crops from '../generated/crops.json';
import { appVersion } from '../lib/site';
import SiteHeader from './SiteHeader.astro';
import logoSvg from '../assets/logo.svg?raw';
const version = appVersion();
---
<SiteHeader home />

<main id="top">
<section class="hero" id="hero" aria-labelledby="h1">
  <canvas id="field" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <p class="pill"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Amber means a session needs you</p>
  <h1 id="h1"><span class="l">Every Claude Code session.</span> <span class="l">One <em>calm</em> wall.</span></h1>
  <p class="sub">See who is busy and who needs you. Press <span class="inl">a</span> to answer. tmux keeps every session alive.</p>
  <div class="cta">
    <button class="copybox" data-copy="npx claude-garage"><span><span class="p" aria-hidden="true">$ </span>npx claude-garage</span><span class="c"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2.5"/><path d="M5 15V6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 7.5 4H15"/></svg><span class="lbl">Copy</span></span></button>
    <a class="btn btn-line" href="https://github.com/adar2378/claude-garage" data-star><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2.8l2.9 5.9 6.5.9-4.7 4.6 1.1 6.5L12 17.6l-5.8 3.1 1.1-6.5-4.7-4.6 6.5-.9z"/></svg><span>Star on GitHub</span><b class="sh-count" data-star-count hidden></b></a>
    <a class="tlink" href="/try/">Try it in your browser <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
  </div>
  <p class="note">Local only: no account, no telemetry. Needs tmux 3.2+ and Claude Code. macOS and Linux, Windows in preview. MIT. <a href="/docs/guides/install/">Install guide</a></p>
  <div class="hwin" id="hwin">
    <div class="term"><div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span id="hwt">claude-garage</span>
      <button class="abtn" id="hattach" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Attach to the session that needs you"><kbd>a</kbd><span class="lbl" id="hlbl">needs you</span></button></div>
      <div class="vw"><svg viewBox="236 450 1204 430" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin slice" role="img" aria-label="The bottom of the claude-garage wall: one session asks Do you want to proceed, and the status strip says someone needs you"><image href="/renders/wall-needs-input.svg" width="1440" height="880"/><image id="himg-e" data-href="/renders/wall-engaged.svg" width="1440" height="880"/></svg></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== definition: plain text, quotable on its own ===== -->
<section class="def" aria-labelledby="def-h">
  <h2 id="def-h" class="sr">What is claude-garage?</h2>
  <p>claude-garage is a free, open-source terminal app (MIT license) that shows all your Claude Code sessions on one wall, grouped by project. Sessions run in tmux, so they survive closing the terminal. The session waiting for your answer turns amber; press <span class="inl">a</span> to jump to it. It runs on macOS and Linux, with a Windows preview. Made by <a href="/about/">Saiful Islam (Adar)</a>.</p>
</section>

<!-- ===== pinned story ===== -->
<section class="story" id="story" aria-labelledby="story-h">
  <h2 id="story-h" class="sr">How claude-garage works, in five steps</h2>
  <div class="stage-pin">
    <div class="stage mesh">
      <i class="b1"></i><i class="b2"></i><i class="b3"></i><i class="b4"></i><i class="b5"></i>
      <div class="center">
        <div class="stepper" role="tablist" aria-label="Steps">
          <button class="sbtn" role="tab" id="t0" aria-controls="s0" aria-selected="true" aria-label="Step 1: Start"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 8l4.5 4L5 16M12.5 17H19"/></svg></button>
          <button class="sbtn" role="tab" id="t1" aria-controls="s1" aria-selected="false" aria-label="Step 2: See them all" tabindex="-1"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="4" y="4" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="13" y="4" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="4" y="13" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="13" y="13" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/></svg></button>
          <button class="sbtn" role="tab" id="t2" aria-controls="s2" aria-selected="false" aria-label="Step 3: Spot the amber one" tabindex="-1"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3.2" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8"/><path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M2 12h2M20 12h2" /></svg></button>
          <button class="sbtn" role="tab" id="t3" aria-controls="s3" aria-selected="false" aria-label="Step 4: Press a and answer" tabindex="-1"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3.5" y="3.5" width="17" height="17" rx="5"/><text x="12" y="16.4" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Geist Mono,monospace" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor" stroke="none">a</text></svg></button>
          <button class="sbtn" role="tab" id="t4" aria-controls="s4" aria-selected="false" aria-label="Step 5: Nothing gets lost" tabindex="-1"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M19.5 12a7.5 7.5 0 1 1-2.2-5.3M19.5 4.5v4h-4"/></svg></button>
        </div>

        <div class="deck">
          <!-- 1 -->
          <article class="step on" id="s0" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="t0" data-i="0">
            <div class="copy">
              <span class="chip"><span class="ic"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 8l4.5 4L5 16M12.5 17H19"/></svg></span>Start <span class="num">1 / 5</span></span>
              <h3>Point it at a folder.</h3>
              <p>Press <kbd>n</kbd>, or run <span class="inl">claude-garage &lt;folder&gt;</span>. A fresh Claude Code session opens in its own tile, grouped under its project.</p>
              <a class="more" href="/docs/guides/first-wall/">Your first wall <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="vis v-a">
              <div class="term"><div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>claude-garage</span></div>
                <img src={crops.s0.src} srcset={crops.s0.srcset} sizes="(min-width: 900px) 530px, (min-width: 720px) 48vw, calc(100vw - 120px)" width={crops.s0.w} height={crops.s0.h} alt="A Claude Code session tile in claude-garage, showing a diff and passing tests" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
              <div class="fl fl-tl bob" style="--d:.05s"><code>$ claude-garage ~/acme</code></div>
              <div class="fl fl-br" style="--d:.2s"><span class="key" style="width:46px;height:46px;font-size:21px;border-radius:12px">n</span><span>New session<small>pick a folder</small></span></div>
            </div>
          </article>
          <!-- 2 -->
          <article class="step" id="s1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="t1" data-i="1">
            <div class="copy">
              <span class="chip"><span class="ic"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="4" y="4" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="13" y="4" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="4" y="13" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="13" y="13" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/></svg></span>See them all <span class="num">2 / 5</span></span>
              <h3>Every session, one wall.</h3>
              <p>Each tile is a live Claude Code session. The sidebar groups them by folder, and the status strip keeps your 5h and weekly usage in view.</p>
              <a class="more" href="/docs/guides/many-sessions/">Run many sessions <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="vis v-b">
              <div class="term"><div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>claude-garage</span></div>
                <img src={crops.s1.src} srcset={crops.s1.srcset} sizes="(min-width: 900px) 530px, (min-width: 720px) 48vw, calc(100vw - 120px)" width={crops.s1.w} height={crops.s1.h} alt="The claude-garage wall with three project groups and five sessions" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
              <div class="fl fl-tr bob" style="--d:.05s"><span class="gr"></span><span>3 folders<small>5 sessions running</small></span></div>
              <div class="fl fl-bl" style="--d:.2s"><code>5h 24% · wk 61%</code></div>
            </div>
          </article>
          <!-- 3 -->
          <article class="step" id="s2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="t2" data-i="2">
            <div class="copy">
              <span class="chip"><span class="ic"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3.2" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8"/></svg></span>Spot the amber one <span class="num">3 / 5</span></span>
              <h3>The one waiting on you turns amber.</h3>
              <p>When a tool call needs approval, that tile lights up, its folder gets a dot, and the bar says someone needs you. No tab hunting.</p>
              <a class="more" href="/docs/guides/many-sessions/#how-do-i-know-which-session-needs-me">How the amber signal works <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="vis v-c">
              <div class="term"><div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>claude-garage</span></div>
                <img src={crops.s2.src} srcset={crops.s2.srcset} sizes="(min-width: 900px) 530px, (min-width: 720px) 48vw, calc(100vw - 120px)" width={crops.s2.w} height={crops.s2.h} alt="The claude-garage wall with one tile outlined in amber, waiting for approval" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
              <div class="fl fl-tr bob" style="--d:.05s"><span class="am"></span><span>web needs you<small>Bash command · claude-1</small></span></div>
              <div class="fl fl-bl" style="--d:.2s"><span class="am"></span><span>1 blocked</span></div>
            </div>
          </article>
          <!-- 4 -->
          <article class="step" id="s3" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="t3" data-i="3">
            <div class="copy">
              <span class="chip"><span class="ic"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3.5" y="3.5" width="17" height="17" rx="5"/></svg></span>Press a and answer <span class="num">4 / 5</span></span>
              <h3>Press a. You are in.</h3>
              <p>One key jumps to the session that is blocked, right at its prompt. Pick <span class="inl">1. Yes</span> or tell Claude what to do instead, then carry on.</p>
              <a class="more" href="/docs/guides/many-sessions/#how-do-i-jump-to-the-waiting-session">Jump with a <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="vis v-d">
              <div class="term"><div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>web / claude-1</span></div>
                <img src={crops.s3.src} srcset={crops.s3.srcset} sizes="(min-width: 900px) 530px, (min-width: 720px) 48vw, calc(100vw - 120px)" width={crops.s3.w} height={crops.s3.h} alt="The blocked tile up close: Do you want to proceed? 1. Yes, 2. Yes and do not ask again, 3. No" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
              <div class="fl fl-tl bob" style="--d:.05s"><span class="key">a</span></div>
              <div class="fl fl-br" style="--d:.2s"><code>keys → web/claude-1</code></div>
            </div>
          </article>
          <!-- 5 -->
          <article class="step" id="s4" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="t4" data-i="4">
            <div class="copy">
              <span class="chip"><span class="ic"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M19.5 12a7.5 7.5 0 1 1-2.2-5.3M19.5 4.5v4h-4"/></svg></span>Nothing gets lost <span class="num">5 / 5</span></span>
              <h3>tmux owns your sessions.</h3>
              <p>Quit the wall and they keep running. Closed or crashed chats stay in the sidebar; press <kbd>r</kbd> <kbd>r</kbd> to restart and resume the conversation.</p>
              <a class="more" href="/docs/guides/nothing-lost/">Close and come back <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="vis v-e">
              <div class="term"><div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>claude-garage</span></div>
                <img src={crops.s4.src} srcset={crops.s4.srcset} sizes="(min-width: 900px) 530px, (min-width: 720px) 48vw, calc(100vw - 120px)" width={crops.s4.w} height={crops.s4.h} alt="The sidebar listing closed, crashed and restartable chats next to live sessions" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
              <div class="fl fl-tr bob" style="--d:.05s"><span class="gr"></span><span id="rest">restored 3 sessions</span></div>
              <div class="fl fl-br" style="--d:.2s"><span class="key w" style="height:46px;font-size:20px;border-radius:12px">r</span><span class="key w" style="height:46px;font-size:20px;border-radius:12px">r</span><span style="margin-left:4px">resume</span></div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center">
          <div class="prog" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div>
          <div class="hint" aria-hidden="true">scroll, or click an icon</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== plugins ===== -->
<section class="s" id="plugins">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="eyebrow rv">Ten in the box. Install more from GitHub.</span>
      <h2 class="rv" style="--rd:.05s">Ten built-in plugins, and how to add your own</h2>
      <p class="lead rv" style="--rd:.1s">Plugins are small, switchable add-ons that tune the wall to how you work. The crops below are the real thing. <a href="/docs/guides/plugins/">Read the plugin guide</a> or <a href="/docs/guides/first-plugin/">build your first plugin</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pgrid">
      <article class="pc rv">
        <div class="pv"><div class="mini" style="width:62%"><img src={crops.p0.src} width={crops.p0.w} height={crops.p0.h} alt="Sidebar rows reading claude-3 closed, claude-4 crashed" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div></div>
        <h3><a href="/docs/guides/plugins/#the-ten-built-in-plugins">Closed chats</a></h3><p>Closed sessions stay in the rail. Click one to bring it back.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pc rv" style="--rd:.07s">
        <div class="pv"><div class="mini"><img src={crops.p1.src} width={crops.p1.w} height={crops.p1.h} alt="A tile header with x and del buttons" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div></div>
        <h3><a href="/docs/guides/plugins/#the-ten-built-in-plugins">Tile buttons</a></h3><p>Close and delete buttons in each tile title.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pc rv" style="--rd:.14s">
        <div class="pv"><div class="mini"><img src={crops.p2.src} width={crops.p2.w} height={crops.p2.h} alt="Status bar showing 5h 24% and weekly 61% usage" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div></div>
        <h3><a href="/docs/guides/plugins/#the-ten-built-in-plugins">Usage bar</a></h3><p>Your 5 hour and weekly limits in the status strip.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pc rv">
        <div class="pv"><div class="mini" style="width:88%"><img src={crops.p3.src} width={crops.p3.w} height={crops.p3.h} alt="Status bar with folder tabs and a tiny pet" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div></div>
        <h3><a href="/docs/guides/plugins/#the-ten-built-in-plugins">Pit pet</a></h3><p>A tiny pet in the status strip. It wakes when a session needs you.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pc rv">
        <div class="pv"><div class="keys"><span class="skey">♪</span></div></div>
        <h3><a href="/docs/guides/alerts/">Alerts</a></h3><p>A chime when a session needs you or finishes a long turn, and a desktop banner when garage is out of view.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pc rv" style="--rd:.07s">
        <div class="pv"><div class="keys"><span class="skey">s</span><span class="skey">S</span></div></div>
        <h3><a href="/docs/guides/plugins/#the-ten-built-in-plugins">Quick send</a></h3><p><span class="inl">s</span> sends a line to one session, <span class="inl">S</span> to every session in the project.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pc rv" style="--rd:.14s">
        <div class="pv"><div class="keys"><span class="skey">/</span></div></div>
        <h3><a href="/docs/guides/plugins/#the-ten-built-in-plugins">Jump palette</a></h3><p>Press <span class="inl">/</span> to jump to any session.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pc rv">
        <div class="pv"><div class="ico"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 5v14M12 9v10M19 13v6"/></svg></div></div>
        <h3><a href="/docs/guides/plugins/#the-ten-built-in-plugins">Turn markers</a></h3><p>Marks where each Claude turn ended, right in the tile.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pc rv" style="--rd:.07s">
        <div class="pv"><div class="ico"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 7h16M9 7V5h6v2M6.5 7l1 12h9l1-12"/></svg></div></div>
        <h3><a href="/docs/guides/plugins/#the-ten-built-in-plugins">Prune empty projects</a> <span class="tag">off by default</span></h3><p>Removes a project after you close its last session. Off by default.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pc rv" style="--rd:.14s">
        <div class="pv"><div class="ico"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 8l4.5 4L5 16M12.5 17H19"/></svg></div></div>
        <h3><a href="/docs/plugins/cli/">CLI extras</a></h3><p>Adds <span class="inl">claude-garage &lt;folder&gt;</span>, <span class="inl">open</span>, <span class="inl">install</span> and <span class="inl">prune</span> to your shell.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="install-row">
      <div class="box dk rv">
        <span class="l">Add a plugin from any GitHub repo (<a href="/docs/guides/plugins/">how installing works</a>)</span>
        <div class="cmd"><span>claude-garage plugin install owner/repo</span><button data-copy="claude-garage plugin install owner/repo">Copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="box trust rv" style="--rd:.08s">
        <div class="sh"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5.5c0 4.2-2.9 7.6-7 9.5-4.1-1.9-7-5.3-7-9.5V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2.2 2.2L15.5 10"/></svg></div>
        <div><h3>You stay in charge.</h3><p>A plugin can never confirm a dangerous action. You do. <a href="/blog/plugin-confirm-rule/">How the rule works</a>, and the <a href="/docs/plugins/security/">plugin security model</a>.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== keys ===== -->
<section class="s" id="keys">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 class="rv">The keys you use every day in claude-garage</h2>
      <p class="lead rv" style="--rd:.1s">Press <span class="inl">?</span> in the wall for every key, or read the <a href="/docs/reference/keys/">full key reference</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="kgrid">
      <div class="kc rv"><div class="caps"><span class="cap">r</span><span class="cap">r</span></div><h3><a href="/docs/guides/nothing-lost/">Restart and resume</a></h3><p>Brings a session back and picks the conversation up where it stopped.</p></div>
      <div class="kc rv" style="--rd:.07s"><div class="caps"><span class="cap">x</span><span class="cap">x</span></div><h3><a href="/docs/guides/worktrees/#finish-a-worktree-session">Close a session</a></h3><p>Closes the chat and lets you merge or discard its worktree.</p></div>
      <div class="kc rv" style="--rd:.14s"><div class="caps"><span class="cap">/</span></div><h3><a href="/docs/guides/plugins/#the-ten-built-in-plugins">Jump palette</a></h3><p>Fuzzy-jump to any session without leaving the keyboard.</p></div>
      <div class="kc rv" style="--rd:.21s"><div class="caps"><span class="cap">s</span><span class="cap">S</span></div><h3><a href="/docs/guides/plugins/#the-ten-built-in-plugins">Send a line</a></h3><p><span class="inl">s</span> to one session, <span class="inl">S</span> to all of them at once.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== how it differs ===== -->
<section class="s" id="differs">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 class="rv">How claude-garage differs from other ways to run Claude Code sessions</h2>
      <p class="lead rv" style="--rd:.05s">claude-garage runs Claude Code only, on tmux, and is built for the moment one session waits for you. Other tools cover more agents, more machines or a full desktop app. Each comparison says when the other option is the better pick. The author of claude-garage wrote them, and says so.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cmp rv">
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/compare/many-terminal-tabs/">vs many terminal tabs</a></li>
        <li><a href="/compare/tmux-alone/">vs tmux on its own</a></li>
        <li><a href="/compare/ide-agent-panels/">vs IDE agent panels</a></li>
        <li><a href="/compare/one-session-at-a-time/">vs one session at a time</a></li>
        <li><a href="/compare/claude-garage-vs-claude-code-agent-view/">vs Claude Code's agent view</a></li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn btn-line sm" href="/compare/alternatives/">Compare with other session managers <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== install ===== -->
<section class="s" id="install">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="eyebrow rv">One line to your first wall.</span>
      <h2 class="rv" style="--rd:.05s">Install claude-garage with npx or a shell installer</h2>
      <p class="lead rv" style="--rd:.1s">Try it with npx, or install the binary. Pick your shell. Full steps, troubleshooting and uninstall are in the <a href="/docs/guides/install/">install guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="inst rv">
      <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Install method">
        <button class="tab" role="tab" id="i0" aria-controls="p0" aria-selected="true">npx</button>
        <button class="tab" role="tab" id="i1" aria-controls="p1" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">macOS / Linux</button>
        <button class="tab" role="tab" id="i2" aria-controls="p2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">PowerShell</button>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="p0" aria-labelledby="i0">
        <div class="l">Needs Node.js 20 or newer. Nothing else to install first.</div>
        <div class="cmd"><span>npx claude-garage</span><button data-copy="npx claude-garage">Copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="p1" aria-labelledby="i1" hidden>
        <div class="l">Shell installer for macOS and Linux.</div>
        <div class="cmd"><span>curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -LsSf https://github.com/adar2378/claude-garage/releases/latest/download/claude-garage-installer.sh | sh</span><button data-copy="curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -LsSf https://github.com/adar2378/claude-garage/releases/latest/download/claude-garage-installer.sh | sh">Copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="p2" aria-labelledby="i2" hidden>
        <div class="l">PowerShell installer. Windows support is in preview.</div>
        <div class="cmd"><span>irm https://github.com/adar2378/claude-garage/releases/latest/download/claude-garage-installer.ps1 | iex</span><button data-copy="irm https://github.com/adar2378/claude-garage/releases/latest/download/claude-garage-installer.ps1 | iex">Copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="facts"><span class="fact">macOS and Linux</span><span class="fact">Windows in preview</span><span class="fact">MIT licensed</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="reqs rv">
      <h3>Requirements</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>tmux 3.2 or newer</strong> on macOS and Linux. Check with <span class="inl">tmux -V</span>. On macOS, claude-garage offers to run <span class="inl">brew install tmux</span> and asks first. Windows does not use tmux.</li>
        <li><strong>Claude Code on your PATH.</strong> Check with <span class="inl">claude --version</span>. <a href="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code">Claude Code install instructions</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Node.js 20 or newer</strong>, only for <span class="inl">npx</span>. The shell and PowerShell installers do not need Node.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== faq: visible text only, no FAQPage schema ===== -->
<section class="s" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
  <div class="wrap faq">
    <h2 id="faq-h" class="rv">Questions people ask</h2>
    <dl class="rv" style="--rd:.06s">
      <div><dt>Is it free?</dt><dd>Yes. claude-garage is open source under the MIT license. You still pay for your own Claude usage.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Why tmux?</dt><dd>tmux runs the sessions, so closing the wall, the terminal or your laptop does not end them. <a href="/blog/why-tmux-owns-your-sessions/">Why tmux owns your sessions</a>.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Does it change Claude Code?</dt><dd>No. It runs the normal <span class="inl">claude</span> command. Only if you press <span class="inl">I</span>, it adds status hooks and a statusline to your Claude settings, after saving a backup.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Does it work on Windows?</dt><dd>It is a preview. There is a Windows build, but it has not been tested on real Windows yet. macOS and Linux are the supported systems.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Does it send data anywhere?</dt><dd>No. No account, no telemetry. The background service listens on <span class="inl">127.0.0.1</span> only.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

